---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';import BeforeAfter from '../components/BeforeAfter';import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
const studies=[{category:'Skin',image:'skin',title:'Tone & texture study'},{category:'Skin',image:'ritual',title:'Hydration study'},{category:'Injectables',image:'skin',title:'Facial balance study'},{category:'Body',image:'desert',title:'Contour & light study'}];
---
<Layout title="Results & expectations" description="Explore illustrative comparison sliders and learn how to discuss realistic aesthetic treatment outcomes. These stock studies are not patient results."><PageIntro title="Subtle is a point of view." eyebrow="Results & expectations" description="A thoughtful plan starts with realistic expectations. Your face, skin and starting point are individual. Your outcome will be, too." items={[{name:'Results'}]}/><section class="container section" style="padding-top:0"><p class="notice" style="margin-bottom:2rem">All comparisons below show the same licensed stock image with different color grading. They demonstrate the slider interface only. They are not before-and-after treatment photographs, patients or evidence of clinical outcomes.</p><div class="tabs" aria-label="Filter illustrative studies">{['All','Skin','Injectables','Body'].map((x,i)=><button class="tab" data-filter={x} aria-pressed={i===0}>{x}</button>)}</div><div class="grid-2" style="row-gap:3rem">{studies.map(s=><div data-study={s.category}><BeforeAfter client:visible image={s.image} title={s.title}/></div>)}</div></section><section class="section sand"><div class="container split"><h2>The right questions<br/><em>make a difference.</em></h2><div class="stack"><p>At a consultation, ask to see consented examples from patients with a similar starting point. Discuss lighting, timing, treatment settings and the number of sessions behind each photograph.</p><p>Ask about less favorable outcomes and potential complications as well. No image can guarantee how your body will respond.</p></div></div></section><CTA/></Layout>
<script>document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-filter]').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',()=>{document.querySelectorAll('[data-filter]').forEach(x=>x.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(x===b)));document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-study]').forEach(x=>x.hidden=b.dataset.filter!=='All'&&x.dataset.study!==b.dataset.filter);}));</script>
